<title>USA: OnGard 1997 order backlog exceeds 1996 revs.</title>
<headline>OnGard 1997 order backlog exceeds 1996 revs.</headline>
<dateline>HAUPPAUGE, N.Y. 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>OnGard Systems Inc said on Wednesday it is beginning 1997 with a $2.6 million equipment order backlog that surpasses its 1996 equipment revenues by 30 percent.</p>
<p>The company expects the increased orders for its sterilization equipment to continue during the first quarter.</p>
<p>OnGard also said it has successfully completed a two-year research and development program in micro-sterilizer technology, an effort which culminated in the signing of a multiyear contract to supply Stork BV, a Dutch conglomerate.</p>
</text>
